Image Blurring in OpenCV

Image blurring (smoothing) is used to reduce noise and remove unwanted details from an image.
OpenCV provides different blur methods:

1. Average Blur (Mean Blur):
    It replaces each pixel value with the average value of neighboring pixels.

2. Gaussian Blur:
    Used in computer vision for noise reduction.

3. Median Blur:
    Best for removing salt and pepper noise.

4. Bilateral Filter:
     Keeps edges while smoothing.


COMPARISON

| Method           | Function                | Use                        |
| ---------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Average Blur     | `cv2.blur()`            | Simple smoothing           |
| Gaussian Blur    | `cv2.GaussianBlur()`    | Noise reduction            |
| Median Blur      | `cv2.medianBlur()`      | Remove salt & pepper noise |
| Bilateral Filter | `cv2.bilateralFilter()` | Smooth + preserve edges    |
